data.content:
I saved the requirements document at `docs/requirements.md`. It's written from the code only, and I haven't run the endpoints beyond the one existing test, which passes.

It contains:
- an overview of the system and its configuration variables (`PORT`, `DATABASE_URL`, `TELEMATICS_URL`, `TELEMATICS_TOKEN`);
- six functional requirements, one per route:
  - list vehicles;
  - register a vehicle;
  - maintenance check (sets `maintenance-due` when mileage is over 20,000);
  - last known position from the telematics provider;
  - legacy monthly report;
  - 404 for unknown routes;
- the vehicle data model;
- non-functional observations;
- nine gaps G-1 to G-9, flagged as likely backlog items;
- open questions for the product owner.

The main gaps to know about:
- **No real persistence:** `DATABASE_URL` is read but never used, so everything is in memory and lost on restart.
- **Crashes:** a maintenance call for an unknown vehicle id, or a malformed JSON body, will throw an unhandled error.
- **No authentication** on any endpoint.
- **"Monthly" report:** it has no month filter and just dumps all vehicles.
- **Unused dependency:** the `request` package is declared but nothing uses it.

My first draft wrongly said `src/telematics.mjs` had a syntax error. The file is valid, and I corrected the document.
